"wushuang98/Direct3D-V3", "dtype": "fp16", "offline": true, "use_alpha": true, "output_prefix": "refined_1536", "file_format": "glb", "stage_mode": "single_stage", "attention_backend": "efficient", "accel_mode": "lossless"}, "title": "Direct3D-V3 refine"}, {"id": 6, "type": "MarkdownNote", "pos": [20, 30], "size": [1650, 330], "flags": {}, "order": 36, "mode": 0, "inputs": [], "outputs": [], "title": "Note", "properties": {}, "widgets_values": ["## Refine your own mesh with Direct3D-V3\n1. **Image:** upload the image the mesh was made from. BiRefNet cuts it out.\n2. **Mesh:** put a GLB or OBJ into `ComfyUI/input` and type its file name, or paste a full path. The mesh must show the same object as the image.\n3. Run. Result: `output/Direct3D-V3/refined_1536_<id>.glb`.\n\nTip: a mesh remeshed twice (`RemeshMesh`, solid, fill 20, 1024) gives a cleaner result than a raw TRELLIS.2 mesh.\n\nRefines the mesh against your image at 1536. About 1 to 4 minutes on an RTX 5080.\n\n**Memory:** up to 13 GB VRAM and 21 GB RAM at 150,000 tokens. Less memory: lower `max_tokens` (`shrink_to_fit` then scales the model down a little) or set `resolution` to 1024.\n\n**More definition:** 15 steps (twice the time).\n\nResult: `output/Direct3D-V3/refined_1536_<id>.glb`, 10 to 35 million faces. Decimate it for games.\n\nNodes by Mstafa-awad, model by DreamTechAI (MIT)."], "color": "#222", "bgcolor": "#000"}], "links": [[1, 2, 0, 3, 0, "BACKGROUND_REMOVAL"], [2, 1, 0, 3, 1, "IMAGE"], [3, 4, 0, 5, 0, "MESH_PATH"], [4, 1, 0, 5, 1, "IMAGE"], [5, 3, 0, 5, 2, "MASK"]], "groups": [], "config": {}, "extra": {"ds": {"scale": 0.8, "offset": [40, 40]}}, "version": 0.4}